    "action": {
      "type": "CREATE_MOC",
      "input": {
        "tier": "TOPIC",
        "title": "Construction and BIM",
        "createdAt": "2026-08-14T18:16:45.000Z",
        "description": "Map of the construction/BIM vertical: domain concepts (IFC, BCF, EIR/BEP, CDEs), market diagnosis, Powerhouse positioning and integration strategy, and the dtbau engagement.",
        "orientation": "Construction is a target vertical for Powerhouse: document-heavy, fragmented, and quantifiably hurt by poor interoperability. This map covers the BIM domain (formats, process documents, platforms), the strategy for entering it (compose with existing tools, own the high-level document layer), and the concrete dtbau engagement.\n\nStart with the domain: [[IFC carries the semantics in BIM]] and the [[six-branch IFC document model]] explain the data; [[EIR and BEP]] govern the process; [[CDE platforms]] host the collaboration. The strategy layer: [[unstructured data over silos]] is the diagnosis, [[high-level business intelligence positioning]] the response, with [[Speckle]] and [[Iframely embedding]] as the integration mechanics. The dtbau demo scenario ties it all together."
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T18:16:45.000Z"
    }
  },
